AB  - The accelerating deployment of renewable energy technologies has intensified the need for advanced, reliable, and sustainable energy storage systems. Battery Energy Storage Systems (BESS) serve as a cornerstone in facilitating the seamless integration of renewable energy sources into modern power grids. However, ensuring the longevity, safety, and operational efficiency of batteries remains a persistent challenge. This review critically examines the emerging application of ultrasound-based diagnostic and monitoring techniques as a promising avenue to enhance battery health management and sustainability. We present an in-depth analysis of ultrasoundassisted methodologies for precise state estimation, early fault detection, and degradation analysis across various battery chemistries, including lithium-ion and next-generation solid-state batteries. Additionally, the potential contributions of ultrasound technologies toward promoting sustainability are highlighted, specifically in minimizing battery failures, extending lifespan, reducing material waste, and supporting circular economy initiatives. Key technical challenges in integrating ultrasound diagnostics into real-time Battery Management Systems (BMS) are discussed, along with prospective solutions and research directions to enable scalable deployment. This review bridges interdisciplinary perspectives from academia, industry, and policymakers, providing a comprehensive roadmap for advancing safer, smarter, and more sustainable energy storage solutions.
