AB  - This paper presents a new laboratory faultinjection automation system tailored for predictive maintenance (PdM) in industrial pumping systems. Leveraging advancements in Industry 4.0, the proposed system integrates a Programmable Logic Controller (PLC), Variable Frequency Drive (VFD), and sensors within an Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT) framework to enable real-time monitoring and fault analysis as well as dataset-building. Central to this system is its capability to emulate industrial setups while allowing controlled fault-injection for generating robust datasets critical for machine learning algorithm development. The study outlines the system's architecture, including hardware and software integration, and demonstrates its utility through experimental validation. The results validate the system's ability to simulate realistic fault conditions, paving the way for advanced PdM strategies in industrial applications.
