AB  - The construction industry, a key sector of the global economy, is undergoing a profound transformation in response to challenges such as low productivity, high environmental impact and the need for greater resilience. The digital transition, driven by the adoption of advanced technologies such as BIM, Digital Twin, IoT and artificial intelligence, is revolutionizing design, construction and management, improving operational efficiency and predictive maintenance. These tools enable more accurate monitoring of infrastructure, reducing maintenance costs, preventing breakdowns and extending the life of buildings. In parallel, the increase in extreme weather events requires the adoption of adaptive buildings, integrating digital innovations and sustainable building practices. More stringent regulations and strategic investments accelerate this evolution, optimizing the life cycle of buildings and reducing environmental impact. Advanced data analysis enables the identification of effective strategies, improving energy efficiency and promoting a more resilient and innovative built environment.
