KW  - LIFE PREDICTION
KW  - RELIABILITY
KW  - STRESS
AB  - Aerospace components are subjected to complex loading conditions during their service life, which can lead to fatigue behavior and threaten aviation safety. This paper introduces a dynamic predictive maintenance strategy based on predictive fatigue damage to address the challenges of maintenance under uncertain conditions. The study begins by focusing on fatigue damage prediction and develops a hybrid prediction framework that combines physical mechanisms with deep learning, which enables highly efficient and accurate prediction of fatigue damage. Building on this, we then propose a dynamic predictive maintenance strategy that incorporates uncertain impacts based on the remaining fatigue damage. To validate the effectiveness of the proposed method, a case study was conducted on an aerospace component-the aero bulkhead. The results show that the method can accurately predict the remaining fatigue damage of the component in nearly real-time during its service life. Moreover, by incorporating impact factors, the dynamic predictive maintenance strategy allows for timely maintenance decisions before failure occurs, effectively mitigating potential risks. The dynamic maintenance strategy outlined in this paper not only optimizes maintenance decisions by balancing cost and reliability but also provides insights into managing components under uncertain damage conditions. Furthermore, it contributes to advancing the field of fatigue reliability and its practical applications.
