AB  - Rapid technology growth of the Internet of Things (IoT) and Artificial Intelligence (AI) are reforming our way of life from its foundation. What do we realize for an affluent society using IoT and AI? It is a matter of great urgency to answer this question. The Japanese Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry (METI) actually changed their policy in 2017, from "Digital First" to "IoT First" [1] as shown in Figure 1. METI hopes that IoT and AI will provide clear solutions to home appliance accident prevention and accurate plant maintenance by making good use of big data on network services.
   [GRAPHICS]
   Every electrical component has the possibility to report many conditions using data measurement sensors, so it is possible to build big data related to the failure of electrical facilities in network services. However, failure modes of almost all electrical parts involve a sudden breakdown without clear signs of degradation. It is not clear what engineering method is applicable for analyzing big data to provide accurate electrical facilities maintenance. This problem should be solved quickly. The solution should lead to the development of a new risk analysis methodology for electrical facilities maintenance.
   This paper summarizes the research progress of diagnostic and prognostic techniques for electrical components first, and Prognostics and Health Management (PHM) of one candidate technology for this research is introduced. This paper discusses the near future goal of plant mechanical facilities maintenance by applying IoT and AI in Japan, and then clarifies the engineering problem for electrical facilities maintenance. This paper further discusses that the latest risk analysis research cases in four engineering fields. Finally, a new research plan for risk-based maintenance (RBM) methodology applying IoT to electrical facilities is proposed.
