AB  - The integration of artificial intelligence (AI) with green hydrogen technologies represents a transformative approach to achieving decarbonized, resilient, and efficient energy systems within smart cities. Green hydrogen, produced via electrolysis powered by renewable sources, offers a zero-emission alternative to fossil fuels for sectors such as transportation, industry, and power generation. However, realizing its full potential requires overcoming challenges related to efficiency, scalability, cost, and infrastructure complexity. The viability of green hydrogen by enabling predictive analytics, real-time control, and system-wide optimization is facilitated by the use of AI. This paper explores how AI facilitates improvements across the hydrogen value chain from production forecasting and dynamic electrolyzer control to predictive maintenance, intelligent storage and distribution, and demand-side integration within smart grids. Applications in smart mobility, infrastructure decarbonization, and urban planning are discussed, alongside benefits such as increased energy efficiency, reduced operational expenses, improved scalability, and enhanced sustainability. The paper also addresses key challenges, including data availability, cybersecurity, interoperability, and regulatory frameworks, offering research opportunities and policy considerations. Finally, the future outlook emphasizes the need for AI-tailored hydrogen models, digital twin ecosystems, and self-healing energy networks. The synergy between AI and green hydrogen will be instrumental in advancing smart cities toward climate neutrality and long-term energy resilience.
