AB  - Traditional Integrated Circuit (IC) testing methods rely on external testers and predefined test patterns, which are becoming increasingly inadequate as semiconductor complexity grows. The demand for higher reliability, functional safety, and lifecycle efficiency necessitates a shift toward more autonomous and intelligent testing approaches. Embedding intelligence directly into silicon enables real-time diagnostics, adaptive optimization, and predictive maintenance, addressing the limitations of conventional tester-dependent methodologies. This paper explores self-aware silicon and its role in the overall Silicon Lifecycle Management. By leveraging on-chip sensors and Electronic Design Automation methodologies for advanced CMOS technology nodes, self-aware silicon facilitates continuous monitoring, anomaly detection, and intelligent decision-making within ICs. These innovations enhance reliability, optimize performance, and reduce costly failures throughout the silicon lifecycle.
