KW  - Monitoring Data
KW  - Data Analytics
AB  - This research analyzes historical data from the ASTRI-Horn, a Cherenkov telescope located at the Astrophysical Observatory of Catania (Serra La Nave, Mt. Etna). We studied data from various sensors spread across the telescope, which monitor different parameters such as currents, voltages, phases, positions, temperatures, torques, and statuses from several telescope components (motors, encoders, breaks, etc.) as well as environmental conditions (temperature, humidity, wind speed, solar radiation, etc.). Monitoring this extensive set of properties has required sophisticated software architectures exploiting advanced Internet of Things (IoT) and big data technologies. While traditionally, sensor data have been used to correct systematic errors in scientific measurements, this study explores their potential to inform advanced maintenance strategies. Seven years of operational data have been analyzed to identify precursors indicative of component degradation. The aim was to discern unique data patterns or "signatures" corresponding with periods of component damage or replacement. These identified signatures will be instrumental in the development of a Predictive Maintenance (PdM) model, which will aim to foresee the standard operational patterns, issuing alerts for any detected anomalies or deviations, thereby facilitating early anomaly detection and resolution. PdM is an advanced maintenance strategy that, unlike traditional methods that rely on scheduled checks or post-damage fixes, uses data to help predict when components might fail. This approach aims to reduce unexpected problems and costs, improving the overall efficiency and reliability of the telescope.
