AB  - The study aims to systematically and effectively aid in the decision-making for the repair by diagnosing the machinery faults at the component level. It improves operational effectiveness and safety and reduces the chances of critical failures, especially in variable-speed centrifugal pumps, which are beneficial in conserving energy. The study focuses on improving the pump systems' reliability using sophisticated advanced vibration monitoring that facilitates early fault identification. An experimental framework individually tested three common faults-imbalance, misalignment, and mechanical looseness-in controlled environments to study their vibration signatures. Data validation was performed by comparing it with other academic works, validating its correctness. The results of this study shift the paradigm towards a proactive, data-driven approach to routine maintenance, while establishing a dependable framework for predictive maintenance and fault detection, addressing the industrial need for robust, non-intrusive heavy machinery that supports reduced system downtime and uninterrupted operation.
