AB  - As urbanization accelerates and the number of buildings continues to increase, the maintenance and upkeep of structures have become particularly critical; traditional maintenance methods, which predominantly rely on manual labor, are not only costly but also inefficient. In recent years, the rapid development of robotics has led to its growing application in the field of building maintenance, where automation and intelligent techniques have significantly enhanced operational efficiency and safety. In the realm of architectural reverse modeling, achieving intelligent perception of both indoor and outdoor environments is essential for advancing the field; however, reliable scene understanding remains a formidable challenge due to complex structural configurations, dynamic targets, variations in lighting conditions, and occlusions within building environments. To address these issues, this paper proposes a novel scene segmentation approach based on multimodal perception that integrates RGB imagery with LiDAR point cloud data, thereby fully leveraging the complementary strengths of semantic information and spatial geometric details inherent in the two modalities. By employing advanced deep learning techniques, the proposed method markedly improves segmentation accuracy and robustness. Extensive experimental results demonstrate that our approach outperforms traditional single-sensor solutions in fine-grained segmentation tasks across both indoor and outdoor scenarios, maintaining high performance even under complex conditions.
