AB  - This paper presents a real-time people counting and occupancy monitoring system that integrates CCTV hardware with the YOLOv8 deep learning model. The system requires no additional hardware installation and operates solely through software deployment on existing CCTV infrastructure. Designed for institutional environments, the system provides precise entry/exit tracking and workspace occupancy analytics through a responsive web-based interface. Users can select cameras, activate live video feeds, and initiate real-time detection via an interactive dashboard. The architecture supports configurable stream adjustments, such as horizontal flipping and detection confidence thresholds, enhancing usability across diverse camera setups. The YOLOv8 model processes live streams to detect individuals and estimate headcounts with high accuracy. Experimental validation using a five-hour dataset showed a precision of 89-94% across different environments and confirmed reliable system performance over extended operation. Results demonstrate the system's effectiveness in improving safety, resource allocation, and facility management in real-world institutional settings.
