LA  - English
CP  - 5th International Conference on Broadband Communications for Next Generation Networks and Multimedia Applications (CoBCom)
KW  - maritime industry
KW  - digital twin
KW  - smart port
AB  - This paper presents the idea of Digital Twins, a novel technology that allows previously unheard-of degrees of simulation, analysis, and control by reflecting actual objects into their digital equivalents. The article starts by giving a thorough overview of digital twins and outlining their diverse kinds, such as prescriptive, descriptive, and predictive models, each of which has a specific function in a variety of businesses. The emphasis switches to how Digital Twins might be used in the maritime industry, namely in port operations. The study examines how real-time data analysis, predictive maintenance, and operational optimization provided by digital twins may transform port management, logistics, safety, and environmental sustainability. Furthermore, it goes into more detail about the processes involved in building Digital Twins, emphasizing the incorporation of machine learning, simulation, data analytics, and Internet of Things (IoT) sensors. Together, these techniques help to accurately replicate physical assets in a virtual environment, which promotes improved decisionmaking. Additionally, there are described several software platforms that can be used to create Digital Twins with their features, interoperability, and integration potential. Software that facilitates the production of Digital Twins and offers schematic views for complex visualization and interaction with the digital models receives particular attention. Essentially, the goal of this article is to clarify how Digital Twins are revolutionizing port operations by providing an understanding of their creation process and the technology that enables it. Through this investigation there are highlighted the major advantages and challenges of implementing Digital Twins in ports, such as increased productivity, decreased operating expenses, and a proactive approach to sustainability and maintenance issues.
